    "done_when": "First reproduce at base: a promotion whose record fails two independent preconditions (for example an unmoved impl together with a passing gate missing its log) is refused for only the first, and the second appears only on a second call; record it as the base arm. Design constraint: preconditions that can be judged independently are evaluated together and reported in one CrewError, listed in the order the sequence checks them today, with the first one's existing wording kept first, so a caller matching on the first refusal still matches. A precondition that cannot be judged until an earlier one holds (for example, one that reads a manifest the earlier check found unreadable) stays sequential, and the manifest says which ones those are and why. When the stored review read a head the manifest's commits do not name, the refusal names that reviewed head as the commit to pass. In a new tests/test_one_refusal_lists_every_precondition.py: one call against a record failing two independent preconditions raises once, naming both; a record failing one precondition raises with its wording unchanged; and the reviewed-head case names the head to cite. The named negative control (the aggregation reverted so the first failure raises alone) is executed and fails the two-precondition case. Measure fallout before declaring complete: run every test file under tests/ that calls crew complete, complete(), or _complete_locked, or matches a promotion refusal, at base and at head, and list them in the manifest. Any id that fails only at head because it asserted the old one-refusal shape is reported by id with status blocked, rather than edited outside the fence. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder; each log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. Run each arm with -n 8 and --timeout=300, each process on a basetemp under /tmp private to it. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed Python paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. An evidence fragment at docs/evidence/fragments/scoring-should-stop-a-promotion/one-refusal-lists-every-precondition.html records the change. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Land followup f-ssp-guards-one-at-a-time of scoring-should-stop-a-promotion as its body states it: crew complete reports every failing promotion precondition in one refusal instead of one per call, and when the manifest's commit list predates the reviewed head, the refusal names the reviewed head as the commit to cite. The S22 currency triage locates the sequential checks at reckon/crew/promotion.py near lines 4025 to 4094 (report at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s22-coord/scoring-triage/report.md).",
